# Prometheus — mandatory Cursor project rule

Before proposing or modifying code, read these repository sources in this order:

1. `AGENTS.md`
2. `docs/VISION.md`
3. `docs/CHANTIER.md`
4. `docs/CARTE_PRODUIT.md`
5. `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md`
6. `CLAUDE.md`
7. the domain-specific docs, latest migrations, tests and implementation files for the task

Do not rely on memory from a previous Cursor chat. Re-read the current repository state.

## Source-of-truth priority

- Product destination and non-negotiable decisions: `docs/VISION.md`
- Current execution order and next allowed task: `docs/CHANTIER.md`
- Journeys, ownership and target permissions: `docs/CARTE_PRODUIT.md`
- Technical boundaries: `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md`
- Engineering discipline: `AGENTS.md` and `CLAUDE.md`

Historical audits are evidence/context only. They never override the current Vision.

If documents conflict, do not silently choose the easiest interpretation. Stop, identify the conflict, and fix the durable documentation in the same PR before relying on it.

## Current execution gate

Read the **CURRENT IMPLEMENTATION GATE** block near the top of `docs/CHANTIER.md`.

That block is the only authoritative pointer to the next allowed implementation task. Do not infer a later task from an old chat, model memory, branch name or stale documentation.

Work on **one subtask only**.

After the PR is green, stop and wait for Jean-Vincent before merge or any next task.

## Branch / PR discipline

- Never implement a feature directly on `new-JV`.
- Start from the latest green `new-JV`.
- Create `agent/pX-Y-short-description`.
- Inspect existing code, migrations, RPCs, RLS, tests and domain primitives before creating anything new.
- Keep one coherent capability per PR.
- Update `docs/CHANTIER.md` and any durable contract docs when the implementation state changes.
- Run all relevant tests and CI.
- Open a PR to `new-JV`.
- Wait until the required checks are green.
- Review the final diff.
- Report what changed, migrations, tests, CI, remaining risks and the PR number.
- **STOP. Do not merge and do not begin the next subtask without explicit user approval.**

## Product invariants

Never violate these to make implementation easier:

- One account, one common data engine.
- Solo/Coached is personal state; Coach is an independent professional capability.
- A Coach can themselves be Coached.
- Personal/Coaching workspace is UI context, never authorization.
- Permissions depend on resource ownership, relationship and action.
- Athlete owns their personal data.
- One active Coach maximum per athlete.
- Marketplace request is athlete-initiated; Coach acceptance alone does not activate coaching.
- Final marketplace activation requires explicit athlete confirmation.
- Coaching relationship has no paused state: pre-activation, active, or ended.
- AI is proactive but never silently applies durable strategic changes.
- Coached strategic adaptations go through the Coach.
- Weekly AI review persists even if check-ins have another frequency.
- Human accept/modify/refuse decisions become AI context.
- Today-only adaptation never silently changes the future program.
- Dashboard = today/overview. Calendar = separate temporal navigation for Solo + Coached.
- Completed history is never silently rewritten.
- No global progression score.
- Progress photos are never analyzed by AI.
- No public Coach star/review system unless Vision changes explicitly.
- Coach without verified qualifications is allowed but receives no verified badge.
- Imports require preview/correction/confirmation when ambiguous.
- Full product export is not currently a planned feature.
- Workout core remains robust offline.
- Solo trial = 14 days.
- Coach payment grace = 7 days.
- Prometheus bills software, not the coaching service; coaching payment stays outside Prometheus.
- Exact prices, Coach tiers and AI quotas are undecided. Never invent them.
- Beta can bypass paywalls but must still measure cost/usage.
- Current sport UX remains focused on strength/bodybuilding/powerlifting/hypertrophy until an explicit expansion project exists.

## Completion standard

A functional task is not complete unless relevant items are green:

- `npm test`
- `npm run typecheck`
- `npm run lint`
- `npm run build`
- `npm run verify:migrations`
- `npm run verify:edges`
- `npm run test:rls` for RLS/RPC/security-sensitive work
- browser/E2E proof when the user journey requires it

Also verify:

- FR/EN parity when UI changes
- mobile/desktop when UI changes
- loading / empty / error / retry states
- offline/network behavior
- no private data leakage into telemetry
- persistence confirmed before success UI
- append-only database migrations
- no weakened authorization just to make tests pass

The goal is not to complete tickets quickly. The goal is to move the codebase toward `docs/VISION.md` without creating new architectural drift.
